WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.250
- So if you could use
artificial intelligence

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.040
like to make your life
easier, what would you do?

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.611
'Cause mine would be
a masseuse. (laughing)

00:00:08.611 --> 00:00:10.320
- That sounds kinda kinky.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.843
- My body. (laughing)

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:14.651
I didn't go there.

00:00:14.651 --> 00:00:15.743
- That's sounds all-purpose.

00:00:15.743 --> 00:00:17.700
Listen, if it happens, it happens.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.651
- Look, I'm not even,

00:00:19.651 --> 00:00:21.120
I don't know how to talk about that.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.320
I'm on daytime right now.
- I'm so sorry.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.153
- No, no.
- It's too early.

00:00:23.153 --> 00:00:25.037
- But no, but I will say, whatever.

00:00:25.037 --> 00:00:29.130
But no, I find myself, I'm 40, like

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.830
and I find myself, I just,
I feel broken sometimes.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.870
And I started Pilates
and did all the things.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.480
A million things, but
like, I just feel broken.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.465
- I love the way you say
Pilates with such disgust.

00:00:37.465 --> 00:00:38.550
- [Kelly] I know, it's like
- You're like Pilates.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.110
- I actually love Pilates, but I'm like,

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:41.310
it's just such a cliche.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.143
You get to a certain age

00:00:42.143 --> 00:00:43.790
and you're like, "I'm going to Pilates".

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:44.641
I'm like, you know, it's, yeah.

00:00:44.641 --> 00:00:45.474
- You do the hand print.

00:00:45.474 --> 00:00:47.760
- And I do the, yeah, stretch it out.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:48.881
But it is wonderful.

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:51.120
But I find that my body always hurts.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.140
So I'd get, I'd have a masseuse.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.150
- You'd have a masseuse.
That's a really good idea.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.410
- What about you? What would you do?

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.629
- I would, so even though
for my entire life,

00:00:57.629 --> 00:01:00.000
three times a day, I've had to eat,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.650
I forget every time

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.779
until it's like an hour
after I'm starving hungry.

00:01:04.779 --> 00:01:07.140
- I do this.
- And I'm like, what is food?

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:08.310
What is food preparation?

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.260
What is planning? What's
the approach here?

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.360
Just someone to just
remind me that it's coming.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.580
- I'm bad at that too.
I think you're too busy.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.440
- Yeah, exactly. I get like
wrapped up in something.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.910
- Yeah. Yeah.
- And you're hungry.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.410
So if I had, and then I mean,

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:20.564
if we're in a world where we're dreaming,

00:01:20.564 --> 00:01:23.160
it's also preparing the food for me.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.110
Because even sometimes
when you're that hungry

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.540
like a mac and cheese seems
kind of insurmountable.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:28.373
- [Kelly] Yes.
- Yes.

00:01:28.373 --> 00:01:29.430
- It's hilarious to me

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.320
how many cooking demos I do on this show.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.580
- [Allison] I know.
- And I'm not a cook.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.080
- I know. I know.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.411
- It's ironic. Really.

00:01:35.411 --> 00:01:36.660
- I relate to you in that way.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:37.713
- Oh yeah, me too.

